notes: V037 remains the owner-requested candidate after V036. R6 replaces the R2/R4 single-lwIP-window adaptation after controlled physical isolation tests disproved the 3.8-5 KB JPEG assumption: camera-only testing was stable with one CAMERA_GRAB_WHEN_EMPTY framebuffer at 20 MHz, and TCP-only testing delivered 8 KiB, 16 KiB and 32 KiB framed payloads with 1040 successful sends, zero send failures and zero Wi-Fi disconnects on the strong AP. R6 therefore keeps the ATL1 length-prefixed persistent TCP JPEG protocol but preserves the user's configured JPEG quality and resolution across transport pressure; automatic q=50 compression, learned payload targets, local oversize rejection and effective-resolution downshifts are removed. The ESP now uses one framebuffer with CAMERA_GRAB_WHEN_EMPTY, keeps 20 MHz XCLK, discards the buffered frame when a new TCP client connects, never queues catch-up frames, and uses relaxed bounded non-blocking send guardrails (700 ms stall / 1500 ms total; longer during connection warmup). RSSI, BSSID, channel and Wi-Fi disconnect/reconnect telemetry are exposed so weak mesh/AP association is visible. Legacy R2/R4 telemetry keys remain present as zero-valued compatibility fields. PC Studio's existing persistent-TCP reconnect/session-recovery worker and V036 protocol compatibility are retained. V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline until explicit owner acceptance changes it. Physical/public-road signal control remains disabled.
